From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Crewship <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 03:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(watch): wake firstmate from the crew board

With the board socket live, the watcher starts bin/fm-board-bridge.sh. It
subscribes to the fm topic, queues one durable check row per message, and the
watcher surfaces it like an inbox note, so the idle wait ends within about 1 s.
The board seq is the cursor, so a successor watcher resumes without loss.
With config/board-doorbell, a task/<id> message also rings that task's pane
through fm_task_inbox_ring. The board off starts nothing and writes nothing.
